# Kbuild for the Rust-for-Linux data path.
#
# Built only inside a kernel source tree with CONFIG_RUST=y. The kernel's own
# build system compiles module.rs against the in-tree `kernel` crate and links
# ufw_kcore as a dependency. There is nothing to build here on a machine
# without such a tree, which is why `ufw_kcore` — the part that matters and the
# part that is verified — is a normal cargo crate that builds and tests
# everywhere.
#
#   Load path (inside a configured kernel tree):
#     make -C /path/to/linux M=$(pwd) rust-analyzer   # editor support
#     make -C /path/to/linux M=$(pwd) modules
#     insmod ufw.ko
#
# The daemon reports whether this module or the C one is loaded; they are
# alternatives, not a stack, and a host runs one.

obj-m += ufw.o

# The Rust module's single translation unit. The kernel build turns module.rs
# into ufw.o; ufw_kcore is pulled in as a crate dependency declared in
# module.rs's use statements and resolved from ufw_kcore/.
ufw-y := module.o
